# Normalize line endings on checkout and commit.
#
# Without this, an editor on Windows that saves CRLF rewrites every line of a file, and
# git reports the whole file as modified even though not a byte of content changed. The
# frontend sources hit this: two JavaScript files came back with CRLF on every line while
# their content was identical, which is indistinguishable from a real edit in `git status`
# and in a diff until you look at the line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF. `text=auto` normalizes on the way in, `eol=lf` writes LF back
# out on every platform, so a checkout on Windows no longer turns the tree into a diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.jar binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary

# Generated lockfiles: normalize but do not merge.
package-lock.json text eol=lf -diff
pnpm-lock.yaml   text eol=lf -diff
